[statement]
A package whose name a package of the resolution takes, where no package
kept or replaced needs that name, is removed among the first removals,
not at its successor's turn: `idf` takes `id` from the installed `ide`,
and nothing installed needs `id`, so apk removes `ide` right after `old`.
Contrast `a-package-losing-a-name-it-provides-is-removed-at-the-turn-of-its-successor`,
where `x` needs `id`.

[repository]
P:ide
V:1
p:id=78

P:idf
V:1
p:id=78

P:app
V:1
D:a b idf

P:a
V:1

P:b
V:1

[installed]
P:old
V:1

P:ide
V:1
p:id=78

P:x
V:1

[world]
x

[request]
app

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
remove old 1
remove ide 1
install a 1
install b 1
install idf 1
install app 1
